  "notes": "The Gen1 Standard 24 spec table prints no PoE row at all: Port Layout \"1 GbE RJ45 24 (1G/100M/10M), 1G SFP 2 (1G)\", Power Method \"Universal input, 100-240V AC, 50/60 Hz\" - no per-port wattage, no budget, no PoE standard. The powered members of the family are separate models with their own budgets (us-24-250w.json 250 W, us-24-500w.json 500 W), so the silence is the product decision. Without `poeIn: false` on its 24 copper sockets `isPoePd()` matched `unifi` in the label and inferred 12.95 W each - **310.8 W**."
